{"name":"Red Devil","hex":"#860111","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Red Devil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["someone connected with Manchester United Football Club, as a fan, player, coach etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Red_Devil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Devil, Alaska","blocks":[{"text":"Red Devil is a census-designated place (CDP) in Bethel Census Area, Alaska, United States. As of the 2020 census, Red Devil had a population of 22. Their post office was founded in 1957."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Red_Devil_Alaska_postmark.jpg/330px-Red_Devil_Alaska_postmark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Devil%2C_Alaska"},{"title":"Ii Naomasa","blocks":[{"text":"Ii Naomasa  was a Japanese samurai general and daimyo under the Sengoku period daimyō, and later shōgun, Tokugawa Ieyasu. He led the clan after the death of Ii Naotora. He married Tobai-in, Matsudaira Yasuchika's daughter and adopted daughter of Tokugawa Ieyasu."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Ii_Naomasa.jpg/330px-Ii_Naomasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ii_Naomasa"},{"title":"Red Devil (interurban)","blocks":[{"text":"The Red Devil was a high-speed interurban streetcar built by the Cincinnati Car Company for the Cincinnati and Lake Erie Railroad (C&LE) in 1929–1930. They saw service throughout Ohio in the 1930s. After the failure of the C&LE in 1939 they saw service with the Cedar Rapids and Iowa City Railway (CRANDIC) and the Lehigh Valley Transit Company. Several have been preserved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/19660813_05_C%26LE_119_Ohio_Railway_Museum-3_%288682437478%29.jpg/330px-19660813_05_C%26LE_119_Ohio_Railway_Museum-3_%288682437478%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Devil_(interurban)"},{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Ii_Naomasa%27s_Monument.jpg/500px-Ii_Naomasa%27s_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Ii_Naomasa%27s_Monument.jpg/500px-Ii_Naomasa%27s_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monument to the birthplace of Ii Naomasa, Ryutanji Temple, Inasa-cho, Hamamatsu City, Shizuoka Prefecture","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIi_Naomasa's_Monument.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Osuga_Yasutaka.jpg/500px-Osuga_Yasutaka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Osuga_Yasutaka.jpg/500px-Osuga_Yasutaka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Osuga Yasutaka, senior Tokugawa general","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOsuga_Yasutaka.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Kunohejou001.jpg/500px-Kunohejou001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm